id: pm-x4wbui
title: Unknown-option refusal textual flags bypass structured global-option filtering
description: CodeRabbit review on PR #1133 found that resolveRefusalCandidateFlag may select the first flag mentioned in guidance prose before its structured provided_fields scan excludes global flags. A message naming --json before invalid --depth can therefore report the global flag and its following argument instead of the rejected option. Apply one admissibility predicate to both paths and prove exact surface/value attribution.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:sdk",contracts,recovery,review-feedback
created_at: "2026-08-27T19:11:44.445Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T14:23:16.918Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-28T14:23:16.287Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-28T14:23:16.287Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Textual and structured refusal candidates share one admissibility predicate; valid global flags cannot override an invalid command option; a regression proves surface --depth and rejected_value verbose when --json is mentioned first; exact coverage and static gates pass
parent: pm-f05lsg
resolution: Unknown-option recovery now removes a rejected spelling only when it appears exactly once; repeated occurrences publish no automatic retry.
expected_result: Every advertised shell-free retry removes the complete rejected option condition or refuses to speculate.
actual_result: "A repeated invalid option no longer yields a retry containing the same invalid option, while explicit corrections and unambiguous single occurrences remain supported."
